01:05:34.090 --> 01:05:35.370
She played Rachel Brooks.
她扮演的是雷切尔·布鲁克斯。

1664
01:05:36.130 --> 01:05:38.390
Erika is a classically trained actress.
埃里卡是一位受过正统训练的演员。

1665
01:05:38.750 --> 01:05:42.430
She graduated with an MFA from the NYU acting program.
她毕业于纽约大学表演专业，获得艺术硕士学位。

1666
01:05:42.890 --> 01:05:47.250
Her professional acting debut was at the New York Shakespeare Festival.
她的职业表演首秀是在纽约莎士比亚节上。

1667
01:05:48.050 --> 01:05:52.490
And since we've been tracking these things, I'll have you know she was not on Monk,
既然我们一直在追踪这些事，我得告诉你她没有演过《神探阿蒙》，

1668
01:05:52.650 --> 01:05:57.430
but she has been on both Law & Order and Law & Order Special Victims Unit.
但她演过《法律与秩序》和《法律与秩序：特殊受害者》。

1669
01:05:57.670 --> 01:05:59.790
I loved all of her reactions to Andy.
我太喜欢她对安迪的所有反应了。

1670
01:05:59.930 --> 01:06:00.810
They were so perfect.
它们简直太完美了。

1671
01:06:01.170 --> 01:06:04.510
And this whole thing has just completely ticked off Stanley.
而且整件事彻底把斯坦利惹恼了。

1672
01:06:04.710 --> 01:06:05.790
He's like, what are you doing?
他就像是，你在干什么？

1673
01:06:05.850 --> 01:06:07.410
He pulls Andy aside.
他把安迪拉到一边。

1674
01:06:07.830 --> 01:06:10.470
And Andy says he loves Julia with all his heart.
然后安迪说他全心全意地爱着朱莉娅。

1675
01:06:10.870 --> 01:06:11.030
Yeah.
对。

1676
01:06:11.910 --> 01:06:12.730
All his heart.
全心全意。

1677
01:06:13.350 --> 01:06:15.650
Stanley is like, if you really love her, fine.
斯坦利的意思是，如果你真的爱她，行吧。

1678
01:06:15.650 --> 01:06:17.110
Give me two of your clients.
把你的两个客户让给我。

1679
01:06:17.310 --> 01:06:18.550
You can have this client.
你可以拿走这个客户。

1680
01:06:18.890 --> 01:06:19.350
Yeah.
对。

1681
01:06:19.650 --> 01:06:23.270
So Andy takes over the meeting in a very awkward way.
于是安迪以一种非常尴尬的方式接管了会议。

1682
01:06:24.130 --> 01:06:28.910
He wonders, where should we send your invoices?
他纳闷，我们该把发票寄到哪里？

1683
01:06:29.350 --> 01:06:30.250
To your boyfriend?
寄给你男友吗？

1684
01:06:30.790 --> 01:06:31.050
Right.
没错。

1685
01:06:31.590 --> 01:06:33.050
Because we certainly could.
因为我们当然可以这样做。

1686
01:06:33.450 --> 01:06:34.910
And she's so matter-of-factly.
而她却那么公事公办。

1687
01:06:35.030 --> 01:06:37.610
He's like, no, you can send it to my work address.
他就像是，不用，你可以寄到我的工作地址。

1688
01:06:37.830 --> 01:06:39.110
This is for work.
这是为了工作。

1689
01:06:39.330 --> 01:06:39.650
Yeah.
对。

1690
01:06:39.990 --> 01:06:43.150
But Andy does find out she does not have a boyfriend.
但安迪确实发现她并没有男朋友。

1691
01:06:43.750 --> 01:06:45.270
And then he kind of panics.
然后他有点慌了。

1692
01:06:45.690 --> 01:06:46.790
He's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

1693
01:06:47.150 --> 01:06:49.070
And then he gets advice from Creed.
接着他从克里德那里得到了建议。

1694
01:06:49.270 --> 01:06:49.950
Why Creed?
为什么是克里德？

1695
01:06:50.410 --> 01:06:51.430
I don't know, but I'm-
我不知道，但我——

1696
01:06:51.430 --> 01:06:53.670
Why would you go to Creed for advice?
你为什么会去找克里德要建议？

1697
01:06:54.030 --> 01:06:55.270
Creed's like, say no more.
克里德说，不用多说了。

1698
01:06:55.490 --> 01:06:56.870
Just go in for a kiss.
直接上去亲就行。

1699
01:06:57.110 --> 01:06:58.770
That's how I got squeaky from.
我当年就是这么把斯奎奇弄到手的。

1700
01:06:59.230 --> 01:06:59.530
Yeah.
对。

1701
01:06:59.890 --> 01:07:01.070
I didn't know who that was.
我当时不知道那是谁。

1702
01:07:01.150 --> 01:07:01.890
I had to Google it.
我只好去谷歌了一下。

1703
01:07:01.990 --> 01:07:03.130
Oh, you didn't know who it was?
哦，你不知道那是谁？

1704
01:07:03.150 --> 01:07:03.430
No.
不知道。

1705
01:07:03.690 --> 01:07:03.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1706
01:07:03.890 --> 01:07:04.510
Now I do.
现在知道了。

1707
01:07:04.710 --> 01:07:04.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1708
01:07:05.290 --> 01:07:05.570
Well.
好吧。

1709
01:07:06.310 --> 01:07:07.110
Charles Manson.
查尔斯·曼森。

1710
01:07:07.310 --> 01:07:08.990
She was part of the Manson family.
她是曼森家族的成员。

1711
01:07:09.250 --> 01:07:09.550
Right.
对。

1712
01:07:09.550 --> 01:07:09.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1713
01:07:10.430 --> 01:07:11.250
She went to jail.
她入狱了。

1714
01:07:11.390 --> 01:07:13.190
She tried to assassinate Gerald Ford.
她试图行刺杰拉尔德·福特。

1715
01:07:13.450 --> 01:07:13.610
Right.
对。

1716
01:07:13.810 --> 01:07:14.150
President Ford.
福特总统。

1717
01:07:14.390 --> 01:07:14.570
Right.
对。

1718
01:07:15.050 --> 01:07:19.930
She was not part of the Tate-LaBianca murders, but she did try to assassinate Gerald Ford.
她没有参与莎朗·塔特和拉比安卡谋杀案，但她确实试图行刺杰拉尔德·福特。

1719
01:07:20.350 --> 01:07:22.430
So I guess Creed kissed her.
所以我想克里德吻了她。

1720
01:07:22.710 --> 01:07:25.070
And he says, have I ever steered you wrong, Jim?
然后他说，吉姆，我什么时候坑过你？

1721
01:07:25.330 --> 01:07:25.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1722
01:07:25.690 --> 01:07:26.750
Just go in and kiss her.
直接进去吻她就行了。

1723
01:07:26.910 --> 01:07:27.710
Just do it.
直接上吧。

1724
01:07:27.830 --> 01:07:30.790
That just, you know, that's what you should do.
这简直，你知道的，这就是你应该做的。

1725
01:07:30.790 --> 01:07:36.710
When he called Andy Jim, if you're Andy, wouldn't you think, hmm, there's many reasons
当他管安迪叫吉姆时，如果你是安迪，难道你不会想，嗯，有很多原因

1726
01:07:36.710 --> 01:07:37.670
to her red flags.
对她来说是危险信号。

1727
01:07:38.030 --> 01:07:39.090
There's so many red flags.
有太多的危险信号了。

1728
01:07:39.110 --> 01:07:40.010
So many red flags.
有那么多的危险信号。

1729
01:07:40.170 --> 01:07:43.930
Well, for whatever reason, Andy is going to take Creed's advice.
好吧，不管出于什么原因，安迪打算听从克里德的建议。

1730
01:07:43.950 --> 01:07:45.610
He's going to walk Julia to the car.
他要送朱莉娅去车那儿。

1731
01:07:45.730 --> 01:07:46.650
He forgot his coat.
他忘拿外套了。

1732
01:07:46.810 --> 01:07:48.530
Could he run back in and get it real quick?
他能跑回去飞快地拿一下吗？

1733
01:07:48.990 --> 01:07:50.490
Because he's very, very cold.
因为他非常非常冷。

1734
01:07:50.810 --> 01:07:53.110
Julia says, my car's right here, I think.
朱莉娅说，我的车就在这儿，我想是的。

1735
01:07:53.550 --> 01:07:55.530
Thanks for walking me down, but I'm good.
谢谢你送我下来，不过我自己行。

1736
01:07:55.750 --> 01:07:59.510
And then when he gets her to the car, he goes in for a kiss.
然后当他把她送到车旁时，他凑过去想亲吻她。

1737
01:08:00.070 --> 01:08:02.010
Andy, come on.
安迪，拜托。

1738
01:08:02.190 --> 01:08:04.510
This woman has had to put up with so much in this meeting.
这个女人在这个会议上已经忍受了太多。

1739
01:08:04.690 --> 01:08:05.790
And now this?
现在又来这出？

1740
01:08:06.530 --> 01:08:08.670
Also, like, she could write him up.
而且，她完全可以写报告告发他。

1741
01:08:09.110 --> 01:08:09.890
I know.
我知道。

1742
01:08:10.130 --> 01:08:11.750
He could lose his job, Andy.
他可能会丢了工作，安迪。

1743
01:08:12.130 --> 01:08:14.110
Don't listen to Creed, Andy.
别听克里德的，安迪。

1744
01:08:14.350 --> 01:08:15.930
They do lose the account.
他们确实丢了这个客户。

1745
01:08:16.130 --> 01:08:16.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1746
01:08:16.450 --> 01:08:17.610
He has a talking head.
他有一段独白镜头。

1747
01:08:17.870 --> 01:08:20.050
So he kind of lost in every way today.
所以他今天可以说是全盘皆输。

1748
01:08:20.310 --> 01:08:22.210
He lost three accounts.
他丢了三个客户。

1749
01:08:22.510 --> 01:08:24.350
He lost two that he gave to Stanley.
他丢了两个转给斯坦利的客户。

1750
01:08:24.550 --> 01:08:24.850
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1751
01:08:24.850 --> 01:08:26.230
One that Stanley gave to him.
斯坦利给他的那个。

1752
01:08:26.450 --> 01:08:28.070
And he kind of showed his ass.
而且他有点出丑了。

1753
01:08:28.270 --> 01:08:28.570
Yeah.
对。

1754
01:08:28.790 --> 01:08:29.030
Yeah.
对。

1755
01:08:29.030 --> 01:08:29.690
He did.
确实。

1756
01:08:30.150 --> 01:08:36.070
Well, speaking of showing your ass, Karen has asked Michael to leave the conference room
说到出丑，凯伦要求迈克尔离开会议室

1757
01:08:36.070 --> 01:08:37.270
and come to her office.
来到她的办公室。

1758
01:08:37.490 --> 01:08:39.310
It's like getting called to the principal's office.
就像被叫去校长办公室一样。

1759
01:08:39.490 --> 01:08:46.370
And he is trying very hard to explain that he had a whole bit with a chainsaw that he
他正极力解释说，他本来设计了一段关于电锯的表演

1760
01:08:46.370 --> 01:08:47.430
hasn't been able to do.
结果没能演成。

1761
01:08:48.370 --> 01:08:50.030
And Karen's like, you know what?
然后凯伦说，你知道吗？

1762
01:08:50.190 --> 01:08:53.570
Why don't you just put it all in an email and I'll send it to my team?
你干脆把这些都写进邮件里，我发给我的团队吧？

1763
01:08:53.570 --> 01:08:56.630
And he's like, I can't put a chainsaw in an email, Karen.
而他说，我没法把电锯塞进邮件里，凯伦。

1764
01:08:56.850 --> 01:08:57.550
I can't do it.
我做不到。

1765
01:08:58.190 --> 01:09:01.750
This is when Pam and Karen are going to have a little bonding moment.
接下来是帕姆和凯伦增进感情的时刻。

1766
01:09:01.950 --> 01:09:02.270
Yeah.
对。

1767
01:09:02.270 --> 01:09:03.850
It's so sweet.
太温馨了。

1768
01:09:04.330 --> 01:09:05.890
Pam says, when are you due?
帕姆问，你预产期是什么时候？

1769
01:09:06.350 --> 01:09:08.690
And Karen says, I'm due in a month.
凯伦说，我的预产期在一个月后。

1770
01:09:09.390 --> 01:09:09.690
Yeah.
对。

1771
01:09:10.290 --> 01:09:12.910
Michael says, who did this to you?
迈克尔说，是谁对你做出这种事？

1772
01:09:13.590 --> 01:09:15.270
Who did this to you, Karen?
是谁对你做出这种事，凯伦？

1773
01:09:15.810 --> 01:09:17.110
She's like, my husband.
她说，我丈夫。

1774
01:09:17.690 --> 01:09:19.050
He's a dermatologiSt.
他是个皮肤科医生。

1775
01:09:19.050 --> 01:09:20.130
We met at a bar.
我们在酒吧认识的。

1776
01:09:20.130 --> 01:09:22.550
And then they have all these cute photos.
然后他们有好多这种可爱的照片。

1777
01:09:22.790 --> 01:09:24.810
They have one where they're like dressed like hot dogs.
有一张是他们打扮成热狗的模样。

1778
01:09:25.590 --> 01:09:26.110
Yes.
没错。

1779
01:09:26.110 --> 01:09:27.410
A hot dog and a hamburger.
一个热狗和一个汉堡。

1780
01:09:27.970 --> 01:09:29.210
It's very cute.
非常可爱。

1781
01:09:29.510 --> 01:09:32.290
We had a lot of fan questions about this.
我们收到了很多粉丝关于这部分的提问。

1782
01:09:32.830 --> 01:09:35.690
Everyone wants to know who is the man in the photo?
大家都想知道照片里的男人是谁？

1783
01:09:35.690 --> 01:09:40.130
Who is Dan, the dermatologist who is married to Karen?
那个娶了凯伦的皮肤科医生丹是谁？

1784
01:09:40.670 --> 01:09:43.890
Well, it was played by writer Dan Gore.
其实是由编剧丹·戈尔扮演的。

1785
01:09:44.250 --> 01:09:44.610
Yeah.
对。

1786
01:09:45.070 --> 01:09:47.530
He was a writer on Parks and Recreation.
他是《公园与游憩》的编剧。

1787
01:09:47.530 --> 01:09:51.930
Yes, and he had been working with Mike Schur and Greg Daniels as they developed that show.
是的，当麦克·舒尔和格雷格·丹尼尔斯开发那部剧时，他一直在和他们合作。

1788
01:09:52.110 --> 01:09:56.130
And we had seen him a few times on set and in the writer's room meeting with those guys.
我们在片场和编剧室里见过他好几次，他当时正和那些人开会。

1789
01:09:56.630 --> 01:10:00.590
And he came to set one day when we were shooting on the stages.
有一天我们在摄影棚拍戏时，他来到了片场。

1790
01:10:00.590 --> 01:10:03.090
And he and Rashida dressed up in all these different outfits.
他和拉什达换上了各种不同的服装。

1791
01:10:03.090 --> 01:10:04.950
And they went around and took pictures.
到处走动并拍了照片。

1792
01:10:07.070 --> 01:10:08.110
It was amazing.
太棒了。

1793
01:10:08.290 --> 01:10:08.910
It was amazing.
太棒了。

1794
01:10:09.290 --> 01:10:13.110
Well, you know, now Karen is going to ask about Jim.
好了，你知道的，现在凯伦要问起吉姆了。

1795
01:10:13.810 --> 01:10:14.250
Yes.
是的。

1796
01:10:14.250 --> 01:10:18.970
It's a little bit of tension, but Pam says we're engaged.
气氛有点紧张，但帕姆说我们订婚了。

1797
01:10:19.250 --> 01:10:22.490
And Karen is just earnestly happy for them.
凯伦是真心替他们感到高兴。

1798
01:10:23.250 --> 01:10:24.690
Rashida really sold it.
拉什达演得真好。

1799
01:10:24.790 --> 01:10:27.130
Because I think as an audience, you're like, oh, what's that?
因为我想作为观众，你会想，哦，那是什么情况？

1800
01:10:27.210 --> 01:10:29.870
And she's like, she has so moved on.
而她表现得好像已经完全放下了。

1801
01:10:30.030 --> 01:10:31.170
She has a whole life.
她有完整的生活。

1802
01:10:31.210 --> 01:10:32.270
She's happy.
她很幸福。

1803
01:10:32.270 --> 01:10:34.850
And it gives Pam closure.
这也能让帕姆释怀。

1804
01:10:35.530 --> 01:10:35.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1805
01:10:36.510 --> 01:10:49.330
I don't know about you, Ange, but I am happy if someone I have broken up with finds, like, a new relationship with someone else and they're in love.
安吉，我不知道你怎么想，但如果我和前任分手后，对方找到了新恋情并且坠入爱河，我是会替他们高兴的。

1806
01:10:49.890 --> 01:10:52.290
Because I'm like, yeah, that's why we broke up.
因为我会觉得，对啊，这就是我们当初分手的原因。

1807
01:10:52.350 --> 01:10:53.990
Because we weren't a match.
因为我们不合适。

1808
01:10:54.110 --> 01:10:55.290
And then you found your match.
然后你找到了你的真命天子。

1809
01:10:55.430 --> 01:10:57.870
I don't have a lot of hard feelings about stuff.
我对很多事情其实都没什么怨恨。

1810
01:10:58.010 --> 01:11:00.770
And I've had some messy breakups, you know?
而且我也经历过一些乱七八糟的分手，你知道吧？

1811
01:11:00.770 --> 01:11:02.870
And even still, I don't know.
即便如此，我也不知道。

1812
01:11:03.070 --> 01:11:05.470
I just, I think I am more Karen on this one.
我只是，我觉得在这件事上我更像凯伦。

1813
01:11:05.570 --> 01:11:06.290
I'm like, well, great.
我会觉得，行吧，太好了。

1814
01:11:06.350 --> 01:11:07.710
I'm glad that worked out.
我很高兴事情能圆满解决。

1815
01:11:07.830 --> 01:11:09.910
Because, you know, good.
因为，你知道的，挺好的。

1816
01:11:10.170 --> 01:11:10.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1817
01:11:10.790 --> 01:11:13.070
It wasn't meant to be for me and Jim.
我和吉姆注定是有缘无分。

1818
01:11:13.270 --> 01:11:14.790
But it's for you and Jim.
但你和吉姆就是天作之合。

1819
01:11:14.970 --> 01:11:15.250
Right.
没错。

1820
01:11:15.930 --> 01:11:17.630
No, I think life is short.
不，我觉得人生苦短。

1821
01:11:17.830 --> 01:11:20.610
My grandmother used to always say, every pot has its lid.
我外婆以前常说，锅配锅，盖配盖。

1822
01:11:20.830 --> 01:11:21.210
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1823
01:11:21.370 --> 01:11:23.210
And I want everyone to find their lid.
我希望每个人都能找到自己的另一半。

1824
01:11:23.490 --> 01:11:23.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1825
01:11:24.210 --> 01:11:25.370
I wasn't your lid.
我不是你的盖子。

1826
01:11:25.490 --> 01:11:26.370
I fell in the water.
我掉进水里了。

1827
01:11:26.870 --> 01:11:28.070
Or I was too big.
或者我太大了。

1828
01:11:28.370 --> 01:11:29.650
I was too big for your pot.
我对你的锅来说太大了。

1829
01:11:29.650 --> 01:11:30.210
Yeah.
对。

1830
01:11:30.670 --> 01:11:31.690
Or too small for your pot.
或者对你的锅来说太小了。

1831
